{"id": "EUVD-2026-27630", "enisaUuid": "188f594c-8076-3466-b5bd-520c2f719b44", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: brcmfmac: validate bsscfg indices in IF events\n\nbrcmf_fweh_handle_if_event() validates the firmware-provided interface\nindex before it touches drvr->iflist[], but it still uses the raw\nbsscfgidx field as an array index without a matching range check.\n\nReject IF events whose bsscfg index does not fit in drvr->iflist[]\nbefore indexing the interface array.\n\n[add missing wifi prefix]", "datePublished": "2026-05-06T07:40:37", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T19:06:13", "baseScore": 8.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b329fbcf075949a038045d8e9b86ae3d5bbd8a54", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2ae3ccb78c0a9ef5ee3d80d02ab319ac1d5af734", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9c81bcc2c695e0082012a2a3d36a0eefaa51579c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3ec7437e9d11374105c2c4e47ae671537729d7e6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9fca68c2512a362cad258e4df12a307bb2ee4b8e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1ae1e1caa428844e481231f6dbe9b4f475f1d52d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b427c2b05222db36d32ee141609de6128e9091bb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/304950a467d83678bd0b0f46331882e2ac23b12d"], "aliases": ["GHSA-24vc-pxrh-rpjv", "CVE-2026-43110"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.27, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "06f37864-2773-335d-9126-ffa4b56a9bb2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2880b86859967af710c72f7d34fb421a86a71e22 <9fca68c2512a362cad258e4df12a307bb2ee4b8e"}, {"id": "088782e9-ad35-379a-ade5-6bb037463732", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3.9"}, {"id": "1a60795a-0004-323e-aab6-d83ad1570096", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.24"}, {"id": "1da0e89b-9b20-3